title Cassette bound (stereo card that records at 44.1 kHz only): Opus is dimmed (the four Opus presets and the Opus codec) with the reason, never resampled; Enter on it shows 'Not available: ...' and stays; FLAC can be chosen; the Sample rate row has the one rate
sizes 480x320 320x480 640x480
ppmm 608
env CASSETTE_DEMO 1
env CASSETTE_DEMO_HOME demo-home
env CASSETTE_DEMO_CARD stereo
env CASSETTE_DEMO_CODECS both
env CASSETTE_LAYOUT_CHECK 1

wait 1500
key s
wait 500
key down
key down
key enter
wait 500
expect text "Opus needs 8, 12, 16, 24 or 48 kHz; this card has 44.1 kHz"
expect text "Sizes for 44.1 kHz, 16-bit, this card"
shot picker-top
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
key down
key down
key enter
wait 300
expect text "Not available: Opus needs 8, 12, 16, 24 or 48 kHz; this card has 44.1 kHz"
shot picker-notice
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
key up
key enter
wait 500
expect text "FLAC"
expect text "44.1 kHz"
say Enter on FLAC chose it (set_rec_params flac) and the page went back
shot settings-flac
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
expect noquit
